On Mon, 13 Jun 2005, David Tillotson wrote:

> There are a couple of things that I think would make explore mode better for
> the player who has the early to middle parts of the game worked out (or thinks
> they have) but still needs a few tries to work out the late game.
>
> One would be a second-chance for explore mode after death. You die, you are
> recorded, then you get an option to resurrect and continue in explore mode

Jukka has written a patch for this. The DevTeam need just to integrate it
into the main code.

> For a similar reason I would like to have an "explore mode save" available.
> This would allow you to continue playing normally after saving, but with the
> catch that the saved game would be in explore mode.

In which situation would you use it? Before drink-testing a potion or like
suicidal actions? These actions need not to be encouraged by fall-back
mechanisms, IMHO. Or before strategical decisions, e. g., whether to
convert an attended altar? I'm not sure this feature would be used widely.

